id":"RelDgSAsUk0P6CQfA0EmX","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 60 — Fortune","body":"Kvothe navigates admissions, Devi's interest, Fishery work, music, and his search for Denna.\n\n- **Fortune** — Kvothe navigates admissions, Devi's interest, Fishery work, music, and his search for Denna.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320865},{"id":"SUxzrZ9gh0fkSQph-JqJr","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 36 — Less Talents","body":"Kvothe astonishes the nine masters during admissions and manipulates the interview into a negative tuition.\n\n- **Less Talents** — Kvothe astonishes the nine masters during admissions and manipulates the interview into a negative tuition.\n- **Kvothe Faces Admissions** — Barefoot and nearly penniless, Kvothe astonishes the masters during his entrance examination.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320841},{"id":"TC6cs_62J1I3g2N2LO-tR","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 54 — A Place to Burn","body":"At the Eolian, Kvothe performs the Lay of Sir Savien while an unseen woman joins after Ambrose breaks a string.\n\n- **A Place to Burn** — At the Eolian, Kvothe performs the Lay of Sir Savien while an unseen woman joins after Ambrose breaks a string.\n- **Kvothe Enters the Eolian** — Kvothe stakes his future on an audition at Imre's most prestigious music hall.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320859},{"id":"TG-IqbLl1K8RJYEwniUW3","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 80 — Touching Iron","body":"The drugged draccus charges Trebon; Kvothe controls the fires and drops the church's iron wheel onto it.\n\n- **Touching Iron** — The drugged draccus charges Trebon; Kvothe controls the fires and drops the church's iron wheel onto it.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320885},{"id":"TWMY7RKQCZ_Z8mRD8BNtU","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 71 — Strange Attraction","body":"Kvothe buys a supposedly black horse, uncovers the swindle, trades with a tinker, and reaches Trebon to find Denna.\n\n- **Strange Attraction** — Kvothe buys a supposedly black horse, uncovers the swindle, trades with a tinker, and reaches Trebon to find Denna.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320876},{"id":"UkEWtEbgCc34U_BuETG2z","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 21 — Basement, Bread and Bucket","body":"Kvothe finds Trapis's cellar, earns bread through work, and discovers one fragile refuge in Waterside.\n\n- **Basement, Bread and Bucket** — Kvothe finds Trapis's cellar, earns bread through work, and discovers one fragile refuge in Waterside.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320826},{"id":"VGDdpXjPs-VOLsmHogDa4","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 53 — Slow Circles","body":"Playing alone in a courtyard, Kvothe befriends the mysterious girl beneath the University and names her Auri.\n\n- **Slow Circles** — Playing alone in a courtyard, Kvothe befriends the mysterious girl beneath the University and names her Auri.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320858},{"id":"VKY5YpwyniylHo4Xu7cnL","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 76 — The Mating Habits of the Common Draccus","body":"Kvothe identifies the draccus from Chronicler's book as an ancient herbivore with iron scales.\n\n- **The Mating Habits of the Common Draccus** — Kvothe identifies the draccus from Chronicler's book as an ancient herbivore with iron scales.\n- **The Beast Is a Draccus** — Kvothe identifies the huge reptile as a common draccus made dangerous by denner resin.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320881},{"id":"VTvMPnMuIA-BfGmgh8CwZ","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 6 — The Price of Remembering","body":"Chronicler reveals his purpose, and Kote agrees to dictate his life only if the account receives three full days.\n\n- **The Price of Remembering** — Chronicler reveals his purpose, and Kote agrees to dictate his life only if the account receives three full days.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320811},{"id":"VXvZOjt_toFmsvgZPueQC","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 74 — Waystone","body":"Kvothe and Denna camp atop greystones and see a huge fire-breathing draccus.\n\n- **Waystone** — Kvothe and Denna camp atop greystones and see a huge fire-breathing draccus.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320879},{"id":"VkuhSbkkuJnSW6S9Ty98A","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 48 — Interlude: A Silence of a Different Kind","body":"Kote struggles to describe Denna and rejects any attempt to reduce her to a list of features.\n\n- **A Silence of a Different Kind** — Kote struggles to describe Denna and rejects any attempt to reduce her to a list of features.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320853},{"id":"W2dpk02pffzWaieDYBLbS","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 72 — Borrorill","body":"Kvothe and Denna inspect the Mauthen farm and find rusted iron and shattered wood matching Chandrian signs.\n\n- **Borrorill** — Kvothe and Denna inspect the Mauthen farm and find rusted iron and shattered wood matching Chandrian signs.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320877},{"id":"W60UbAx9XtU4bX-HNidu4","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 27 — His Eyes Unveiled","body":"Skarpi speaks Kvothe's name as Tehlin authorities arrest him, awakening Kvothe's buried memory and purpose.\n\n- **His Eyes Unveiled** — Skarpi speaks Kvothe's name as Tehlin authorities arrest him, awakening Kvothe's buried memory and purpose.\n- **Skarpi Is Arrested** — Justice Erlus arrests Skarpi for heresy, but the storyteller urges Kvothe to wake fully and leave Tarbean.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320832},{"id":"XVQe-_hiJXMUe1w1zZYEY","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 56 — Patrons, Maids and Metheglin","body":"Kvothe receives silver talent pipes and discovers that the singer who saved his performance is Denna.\n\n- **Patrons, Maids and Metheglin** — Kvothe receives silver talent pipes and discovers that the singer who saved his performance is Denna.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320861},{"id":"XuofkH2vp8GWGR57Cqw6R","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 8 — Thieves, Heretics, and Whores","body":"Young Kvothe sees Abenthy call the wind and persuades the arcanist to join his parents' troupe.\n\n- **Thieves, Heretics, and Whores** — Young Kvothe sees Abenthy call the wind and persuades the arcanist to join his parents' troupe.\n- **Abenthy Joins the Troupe** — After Kvothe sees through his performance, Abenthy joins Arliden's troupe and begins teaching the boy.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320813},{"id":"Y6lkbIQUEscryZXca_9g6","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 13 — Interlude: Flesh with Blood Beneath","body":"Chronicler mistakes Bast for a demon and binds him with iron until Kote forces an uneasy peace.\n\n- **Flesh with Blood Beneath** — Chronicler mistakes Bast for a demon and binds him with iron until Kote forces an uneasy peace.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320818},{"id":"YNz7v4exX6CgV8JkdoGxc","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 70 — Signs","body":"Kvothe hears that blue fire marked a wedding massacre near Trebon and borrows from Devi to investigate.\n\n- **Signs** — Kvothe hears that blue fire marked a wedding massacre near Trebon and borrows from Devi to investigate.\n- **News of the Mauthen Wedding** — Kvothe hears of a massacre near Trebon whose signs resemble the Chandrian.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320875},{"id":"Zd7afRwlT_PvU4FRvza9h","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 58 — Names for Beginning","body":"Kvothe and Denna recognize each other at the Eolian and cautiously renew their connection.\n\n- **Names for Beginning** — Kvothe and Denna recognize each other at the Eolian and cautiously renew their connection.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320863},{"id":"_G4CGDfJIdWE53JpbBrAs","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 57 — Interlude: The Parts that Form Us","body":"Kote tears up Chronicler's first description of Denna and begins again.\n\n- **The Parts that Form Us** — Kote tears up Chronicler's first description of Denna and begins again.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320862},{"id":"eCsF9IKsmcHgumpDpg4FA","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 7 — Of Beginnings and the Names of Things","body":"Kvothe demonstrates Chronicler's cipher, lists the names attached to his legend, and begins with his Edema Ruh childhood.\n\n- **Of Beginnings and the Names of Things** — Kvothe demonstrates Chronicler's cipher, lists the names attached to his legend, and begins with his Edema Ruh childhood.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320812},{"id":"foTEuf9-XcuBg-S-znnle","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 1 — A Place for Demons","body":"Carter interrupts Old Cob's story by bringing a dead scrael to the inn; Kote recognizes that more of the creatures must be nearby.\n\n- **A Place for Demons** — Carter interrupts Old Cob's story by bringing a dead scrael to the inn; Kote recognizes that more of the creatures must be nearby.\n- **Kote Identifies the Scrael** — Kote recognizes Carter's attacker as a scrael and privately understands that it cannot be alone.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320806},{"id":"gyXXDnASNy6Z6tC4_edfE","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 38 — Sympathy in the Mains","body":"Fela helps Kvothe find books on the Chandrian and Amyr before Lorren warns him away from childish subjects.\n\n- **Sympathy in the Mains** — Fela helps Kvothe find books on the Chandrian and Amyr before Lorren warns him away from childish subjects.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320843},{"id":"hNIIETrRDRGcAQCj5SgXH","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 34 — Yet to Learn","body":"Borrowing Josn's lute, Kvothe plays for the caravan and rediscovers the music silenced in Tarbean.\n\n- **Yet to Learn** — Borrowing Josn's lute, Kvothe plays for the caravan and rediscovers the music silenced in Tarbean.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320839},{"id":"hWp2rEDSTDepgdIYvvcSf","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"xvnnlAj5qZ7MIbkXOUF-V","title":"Lanre and Haliax","body":"Lanre returned from death, betrayed Myr Tariniel, and was cursed by Selitos to wear shadow on his face.","tags":["legend","chandrian"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["xXGHlZjaYH3Vpz_9N2EvO","Cx94mPa0244AIMOWOwIYK"],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"i7czqKXekv2MOqkcwm_yT","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 42 — Bloodless","body":"Arwyl discovers Kvothe's preparation while Mola stitches his wounds at the Medica.\n\n- **Bloodless** — Arwyl discovers Kvothe's preparation while Mola stitches his wounds at the Medica.\n- **Kvothe Is Whipped Bloodless** — Kvothe uses an herbal preparation to avoid bleeding during his public whipping, creating a new legend.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320847},{"id":"j94jBTHlDa9uueHJR195D","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"xvnnlAj5qZ7MIbkXOUF-V","title":"The Chandrian","body":"Seven feared figures identified by signs such as blue flame, rust, decay, and silence; they destroy reliable knowledge of themselves.","tags":["chandrian","secret"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["Ti8eZfF6NjTt6Aby_lekt","xXGHlZjaYH3Vpz_9N2EvO"],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"jL6GVOJWeWemTzb13XFcB","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 40 — On the Horns","body":"The masters reduce Hemme's demand for expulsion to three lashes and admit Kvothe into the Arcanum.\n\n- **On the Horns** — The masters reduce Hemme's demand for expulsion to three lashes and admit Kvothe into the Arcanum.\n- **Admissions Sets a Negative Tuition** — Kvothe's performance earns admission and a stipend, an unprecedented result that secures his first term.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320845},{"id":"kC_nUPe2ObTs3cJUcBQLY","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 79 — Sweet Talk","body":"While preparing bait, Kvothe cares for delirious Denna, who reveals that Master Ash gave her bruises.\n\n- **Sweet Talk** — While preparing bait, Kvothe cares for delirious Denna, who reveals that Master Ash gave her bruises.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320884},{"id":"kHCvOpb-WLqJpeKiFnGMm","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 67 — A Matter of Hands","body":"Kilvin explains how he contained the fire while Kvothe learns his rescue has already become legend.\n\n- **A Matter of Hands** — Kilvin explains how he contained the fire while Kvothe learns his rescue has already become legend.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320872},{"id":"kT61rpm83gxaCm8WEdZNJ","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 66 — Volatile","body":"A bone-tar canister ruptures in the Fishery, and Kvothe crosses fire to carry Fela to safety.\n\n- **Volatile** — A bone-tar canister ruptures in the Fishery, and Kvothe crosses fire to carry Fela to safety.\n- **The Fishery Fire** — Kvothe saves Fela and others during a dangerous fire and earns Kilvin's respect.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320871},{"id":"ktq8YyAyoUBk2Wnud05hP","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 65 — Spark","body":"Kvothe balances work, music, friendship, and study while waiting for Denna to return.\n\n- **Spark** — Kvothe balances work, music, friendship, and study while waiting for Denna to return.\n- **Kvothe Builds a Sympathy Lamp** — Kvothe completes a clever blue sympathy lamp in the Fishery.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320870},{"id":"lanC_AHcBYFHPVV6ZTMMK","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 84 — A Sudden Storm","body":"Ambrose breaks Kvothe's lute; Kvothe's sleeping mind calls the wind, and Elodin restores him.\n\n- **A Sudden Storm** — Ambrose breaks Kvothe's lute; Kvothe's sleeping mind calls the wind, and Elodin restores him.\n- **Ambrose Shatters the Lute** — Ambrose breaks Kvothe's lute; grief and rage drive Kvothe to call the name of the wind.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320889},{"id":"loe7OzLUfBpCGlbiZfDry","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 83 — Return","body":"Kvothe returns to Imre, repays Devi, reassures his friends, and worries about Denna.\n\n- **Return** — Kvothe returns to Imre, repays Devi, reassures his friends, and worries about Denna.\n- **Kvothe Kills the Draccus** — Kvothe drops the church's iron wheel onto the rampaging draccus and saves much of Trebon.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320888},{"id":"n-jndzCApyOLEErWUvsm_","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 73 — Pegs","body":"By mirroring Schiem's dialect, Kvothe learns about the Mauthen excavation and strange events near Barrow Hill.\n\n- **Pegs** — By mirroring Schiem's dialect, Kvothe learns about the Mauthen excavation and strange events near Barrow Hill.\n- **Nina Describes the Vase** — Nina recalls a painted vase showing the Chandrian and their identifying signs before it was destroyed.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320878},{"id":"oPwbYTYlowwmGs3M0-d9X","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 29 — The Doors of My Mind","body":"Using Heart of Stone, Kvothe recovers music, sympathy, and the purpose hidden during his Tarbean years.\n\n- **The Doors of My Mind** — Using Heart of Stone, Kvothe recovers music, sympathy, and the purpose hidden during his Tarbean years.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320834},{"id":"ooOIB8HBKZGlmgUuAnlQz","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 25 — Interlude: Eager for Reasons","body":"Bast questions Kvothe's long delay in acting while Chronicler insists the tale unfold on its own terms.\n\n- **Eager for Reasons** — Bast questions Kvothe's long delay in acting while Chronicler insists the tale unfold on its own terms.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320830},{"id":"pVJWifLRj0HGPhkfxF2zF","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 9 — Riding in the Wagon with Ben","body":"Ben recognizes Kvothe's extraordinary memory and begins teaching him the sciences and arts of the Arcanum.\n\n- **Riding in the Wagon with Ben** — Ben recognizes Kvothe's extraordinary memory and begins teaching him the sciences and arts of the Arcanum.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320814},{"id":"qUsPyDYTE__K7Euwq3oq4","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"2GhN-sKSSsRNXdu234l6O","title":"Sympathy and Alar","body":"Sympathy links objects through bindings; its power depends on energy, similarity, and the sympathist's disciplined belief called Alar.","tags":["sympathy","alar"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["yESmakRTZSWXPm8qKw-Ru","xAbQpyK_aLRBM2neEKtAY"],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"qWyeiht9sQD76FpaPnhIh","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 0 — Prologue: A Silence of Three Parts","body":"Three silences define the empty Waystone Inn and its keeper, Kote, a man waiting to die.\n\n- **A Silence of Three Parts** — Three silences define the empty Waystone Inn and its keeper, Kote, a man waiting to die.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"r8Sxk_xJBNJcW-IkifioL","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"9L_3Vt6Mix45Dg0e4y3xi","title":"Skin Dancers","body":"Possessing entities that can seize human bodies and move between hosts.","tags":["skin-dancer","creature"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["XkzG_roCiPb0nyStkR0kk"],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"rmDSh6imI9lLoNNIO8zU6","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 47 — Barbs","body":"Kvothe settles into Artificery and friendship with Wil and Sim while his rivalry with Ambrose escalates.\n\n- **Barbs** — Kvothe settles into Artificery and friendship with Wil and Sim while his rivalry with Ambrose escalates.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320852},{"id":"t3swMJppuNDivNH_tV5m5","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 16 — Hope","body":"Kvothe returns to find his troupe murdered and meets Cinder and Haliax before the Chandrian flee.\n\n- **Hope** — Kvothe returns to find his troupe murdered and meets Cinder and Haliax before the Chandrian flee.\n- **The Chandrian at the Fire** — Kvothe finds Cinder and Haliax among the bodies; the Chandrian flee when unseen watchers approach.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320821},{"id":"t7-697Vm-ZxnNSTPOSyxz","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"2GhN-sKSSsRNXdu234l6O","title":"Sygaldry and Artificery","body":"Runes make sympathy bindings durable and allow artificers to build lamps, clocks, and protective devices.","tags":["sygaldry","artificery"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["pMJ9qMqPS2zS93cMvEq8d","lNxbkwSAdNkTd2bo8NE1i"],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"tqA8Ftpg6zs4hPiItfdAr","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 88 — Interlude: Looking","body":"A possessed mercenary attacks the Waystone, kills Shep, and dies while Kote fails to perform sympathy.\n\n- **Looking** — A possessed mercenary attacks the Waystone, kills Shep, and dies while Kote fails to perform sympathy.\n- **The Skin Dancer Attacks** — A possessed mercenary kills Shep and attacks the Waystone patrons before being stopped.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320893},{"id":"u-7bk5Zmxix37DY84cAjT","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"2GhN-sKSSsRNXdu234l6O","title":"University Ranks","body":"Students progress from E'lir to Re'lar and beyond under the masters, with admissions and tuition reassessed each term.","tags":["university","ranks"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["yESmakRTZSWXPm8qKw-Ru"],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"uO8STktVcHREsmwIbpSP2","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 28 — Tehlu's Watchful Eye","body":"Kvothe retrieves Ben's book, cleans himself, and resolves to reach the University to seek the Chandrian and Amyr.\n\n- **Tehlu's Watchful Eye** — Kvothe retrieves Ben's book, cleans himself, and resolves to reach the University to seek the Chandrian and Amyr.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320833},{"id":"uRX444e4aKUnaBns2tPrE","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 77 — Bluffs","body":"Kvothe and Denna find a dead farmer and discover denner trees whose resin has addicted the draccus.\n\n- **Bluffs** — Kvothe and Denna find a dead farmer and discover denner trees whose resin has addicted the draccus.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320882},{"id":"uV5YZOP3XIygh2S0kJkEX","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 51 — Tar and Tin","body":"Kvothe masters sygaldry, passes his examination, and begins earning money in the Fishery.\n\n- **Tar and Tin** — Kvothe masters sygaldry, passes his examination, and begins earning money in the Fishery.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320856},{"id":"vvr7O6jgFPZBM7inZ6xrn","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 82 — Ash and Elm...","body":"Kvothe learns Denna vanished and hears Nina describe the vase depicting the Chandrian and their signs.\n\n- **Ash and Elm...** — Kvothe learns Denna vanished and hears Nina describe the vase depicting the Chandrian and their signs.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320887},{"id":"w-J6eAAEzEgaebef8zbYM","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 24 — Shadows Themselves","body":"Years later, Kvothe enters a Dockside tavern and hears Skarpi begin the story of Lanre and Myr Tariniel.\n\n- **Shadows Themselves** — Years later, Kvothe enters a Dockside tavern and hears Skarpi begin the story of Lanre and Myr Tariniel.\n- **The Chandrian Memory Returns** — Skarpi's story breaks through Kvothe's trauma and restores his memory of the troupe's killers.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320829},{"id":"w5VERdOa4LCHheI3Iz060","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 89 — A Pleasant Afternoon","body":"Kvothe takes six lashes and spends Ambrose's restitution on a lute, clothes, his blood, and a dress for Auri.\n\n- **A Pleasant Afternoon** — Kvothe takes six lashes and spends Ambrose's restitution on a lute, clothes, his blood, and a dress for Auri.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320894},{"id":"xgr8X9yEvLcbXRHLtNknM","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"9u0DVZY2Ac6K3OcJGeSMP","title":"Trebon and the Mauthen Farm","body":"Mining country where a wedding massacre, ancient pottery, and a drugged draccus converge.","tags":["trebon"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["OFutIzjR2AY8TG0EylcPj","IZBeZ4fKmO1qmy5mtKoc8","JJj7MF31DtzhAjStXHdOt"],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"z8tAqomnWMORkjpLfhoCG","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 31 — The Nature of Nobility","body":"Kvothe uses acting, stolen clothes, and bargaining to outfit himself as a respectable traveler.\n\n- **The Nature of Nobility** — Kvothe uses acting, stolen clothes, and bargaining to outfit himself as a respectable traveler.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320836},{"id":"zF2FJTLynC7jjZysrP8i_","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 90 — Half-Built Houses","body":"Auri leads Kvothe through the Underthing to a hidden Archives entrance, where Fela teaches him the Stacks.\n\n- **Half-Built Houses** — Auri leads Kvothe through the Underthing to a hidden Archives entrance, where Fela teaches him the Stacks.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320895},{"id":"zPPNbFtAookhAxf043pdc","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"9L_3Vt6Mix45Dg0e4y3xi","title":"The Common Draccus","body":"A huge herbivorous reptile whose iron scales and denner-resin addiction make it catastrophically dangerous.","tags":["draccus","denner"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":["StXGN_HbKL85ofKxyi5Ce","EwmFCiNYCi0-rKQiRjRMr"],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"z_4fJUlzNIFDZY-Vn6hYQ","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"lpdEp5VVNrfGvl-oQYAd9","title":"Ch. 22 — A Time for Demons","body":"A Hillside guard beats Kvothe during Midwinter, but a reveler dressed as Encanis gives him gloves, money, and warmth.\n\n- **A Time for Demons** — A Hillside guard beats Kvothe during Midwinter, but a reveler dressed as Encanis gives him gloves, money, and warmth.\n- **Encanis Rescues Kvothe** — A masked reveler dressed as Encanis finds the beaten boy and gives him silver and gloves.\n- **Kvothe Fights Pike** — Kvothe retaliates against Pike with fire, ending their immediate feud at terrible physical risk.","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":null,"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320827},{"id":"wmf-lore-0","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"xvnnlAj5qZ7MIbkXOUF-V","title":"The Cthaeh","body":"The Cthaeh is confined to a tree in the Fae, sees every branching consequence, and chooses words calculated to cause harm.","tags":["fae","cthaeh"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":"wmf-event-104","createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"wmf-lore-1","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"iusifrFL_lfSAAYe7FdIn","title":"The Lethani","body":"The Adem framework for right action is practiced rather than reduced to a simple code. Tempi, Vashet, and Shehyn test Kvothe against it.","tags":["adem","lethani"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":"wmf-event-87","createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"wmf-lore-2","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"iusifrFL_lfSAAYe7FdIn","title":"Adem Hand Speech","body":"Adem conversation combines spoken words with precise hand signs that carry emotion, emphasis, and private meaning.","tags":["adem","language"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":"wmf-event-82","createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"wmf-lore-3","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"xvnnlAj5qZ7MIbkXOUF-V","title":"The Rhinta","body":"Shehyn's account names seven ancient figures whose signs align with the Chandrian known in the Commonwealth.","tags":["chandrian","adem"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":"wmf-event-128","createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"wmf-lore-4","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"xvnnlAj5qZ7MIbkXOUF-V","title":"The Theft of the Moon","body":"Felurian's account connects Jax's theft of the moon to the separation and continuing overlap of mortal and Fae realms.","tags":["fae","moon"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":"wmf-event-102","createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"wmf-lore-5","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"iusifrFL_lfSAAYe7FdIn","title":"Severen's Rings","body":"Courtly rings encode rank, access, obligation, insult, and personal debt. Metal, wood, and bone each carry different weight.","tags":["vintas","court"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":"wmf-event-57","createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"wmf-lore-6","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"iusifrFL_lfSAAYe7FdIn","title":"Tak","body":"Tak is a strategic court game whose highest aim is not merely victory but the creation of a beautiful game.","tags":["tak","bredon"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":"wmf-event-60","createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"wmf-lore-7","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"xvnnlAj5qZ7MIbkXOUF-V","title":"The Lackless Box","body":"The ancient seamless box smells faintly of citrus and iron and resists conventional attempts to discover its contents.","tags":["lackless","artifact"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":"wmf-event-139","createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"wmf-lore-8","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"9u0DVZY2Ac6K3OcJGeSMP","title":"The Sword Tree","body":"The sword tree's razor leaves and unpredictable wind form an Adem trial of movement, attention, and resolve.","tags":["adem","haert"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":"wmf-event-123","createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"wmf-lore-9","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","categoryId":"9L_3Vt6Mix45Dg0e4y3xi","title":"The Shaed","body":"A shaed is a cloak woven from Fae shadow. Felurian makes one for Kvothe after he proves unable to gather the darkness alone.","tags":["fae","artifact"],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[],"visibleFromEventId":"wmf-event-100","createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805}],"factions":[{"id":"1UKuwM_-nfyWprQrN_UoX","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","name":"The Amyr","description":"Legendary order associated with Selitos and opposition to the Chandrian.","color":"#7c3aed","coverImageId":null,"tags":["legend","secret"],"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"6oaB6poaLXRt2Yj5NLBkj","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","name":"Edema Ruh","description":"Arliden's traveling family of performers and the larger culture Kvothe claims.","color":"#b45309","coverImageId":null,"tags":["culture","performers"],"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"8Ejvadw35T_vYQZGhzINa","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","name":"Waystone Household","description":"Kote and Bast's hidden household at the Waystone Inn.","color":"#475569","coverImageId":null,"tags":["frame","newarre"],"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"KePnNL3nkQxQg0CPB8HpF","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","name":"The Chandrian","description":"Secretive Seven who suppress knowledge of themselves and murdered Kvothe's troupe.","color":"#111827","coverImageId":null,"tags":["secret","antagonist"],"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"M6_pfS3rAi_jV_-OsDyKy","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","name":"The University","description":"Students, masters, and staff of the institution across the Omethi.","color":"#2563eb","coverImageId":null,"tags":["school","arcanum"],"createdAt":1785115320805,"updatedAt":1785115320805},{"id":"Q1F4TcXm_wn_iiUwmLks6","worldId":"ag5-SfCGAP0HIVKimJBe7","name":"Tehlin Church","description":"Religious institution with doctrine, priests, and judicial authority.","color":"#dc2626","coverImageId":null,"tags":